 "kind": "trial",
 "note": "Negative trial vs id50 (eligible, distinct normalised source; not a duplicate): one target-independent pre-selector fast path in eik_sigmoid for |x| < 2^-7: returns 0.5 for |x| < 2^-24, else floor(a+1/2) of the affine term a = x*2^22 (x>0, ulp 2^-24) or |x|*2^23 (x<0, ulp 2^-25) in Q15, fast return only when the Q15 fraction exceeds a per-exponent floor of the x^3/48 bound, otherwise the unchanged id50 selector and kernels. Correct on all 2^32 inputs of all three functions (host UBSan/ASan) and on 12 affected sigmoid chunks per target, but S regresses on both boards (rv32im ~1.08x, thumbv6m ~1.12x): the range test runs before id50's first branch on every call (rv32im 4 extra instructions before bltz; thumbv6m ~8 before the original lsls/bmi), and the fast body (~22-26 instr) is slower than id50's own rv32 affine path. See README.md.",
